Spec: Outline hit

Purpose:
  Which rides lie under a tap on the overview map, nearest first.

Owns:
  ./outline_hit.dart
  /test/domain/outline_hit_test.dart

References:
  /docs/decisions/0001-ride-outlines.md
  /lib/domain/ride_outline.sdd
  /lib/domain/route_group.sdd

Must:
  The tap tolerance is `24` logical pixels, turned into metres by the map's zoom and the tap latitude with
    `78271.517 * cos(latitude) / 2^zoom` metres per pixel (MapLibre's 512 px tiles).
  A ride is a hit when the tap lies within the tolerance of any segment of its outline; the distance is that
    of the nearest segment.
  Hits are sorted by distance, then newest ride first; every ride appears once.
  An outline with fewer than two points never hits.
  @OutlineHit.find takes @OutlineCandidate entries (ride id, timestamp, bounds, lazily decoded outline); an outline is
    decoded only when the tap lies near its bounds.
  A hit is marked best when its ride is the best of its @RouteGroup; the hit function takes the best ride
    ids as input and never computes a best time.

Must not:
  Know the map package, pixels on screen beyond the tolerance, or the database.

Scenario: tap on a shared stretch
  Given two rides whose outlines cross the tapped point
  When the map is tapped there
  Then both are hits, the closer one first

Scenario: tap beside a line
  Given a ride whose line is `40` px from the tap at zoom `14`
  When the map is tapped
  Then there is no hit

Example:
  zoom `14`, latitude `0`: `24` px are about `114.6` m
  zoom `16`, latitude `60`: `24` px are about `14.3` m
